  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\n**The ordering guarantee that applies is a single *global* total order — Record A. Record B (per‑consumer positions) is not the contract this integration has.**\\n\\nConcretely: the state‑change feed exposes one durable, monotonic, **filter‑independent position** per committed state revision (Ordarium `change_seq`, `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`). Revisions are delivered in ascending commit‑observation order; every consumer, page and namespace filter draws from that same position space. Consumers may each keep their own cursor *value*, but there is only one position *space*.\\n\\n## What the workspace represents\\n\\nThe workspace is **Palimpsest**, the DSH orchestration plugin, integrating with brother project **Ordarium** (Safe Action SDK / shared ledger). The relevant integration surface is Ordarium's G11 **state kind** and its **state‑change feed** (Ordarium spec `ORD-BOOT-0`) — exactly what the two conflicting records describe:\\n\\n- `docs/engineering/09-ordering-contract-a.md` — global, one position shared by all readers\\n- `docs/engineering/09-ordering-contract-b.md` — per‑consumer, independent positions\\n\\nBoth are self‑labelled \\\"normative, current scope\\",
